{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/841723-rules-about-tattoos","id":841723,"title":"Rules about Tattoos","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-03T22:11:37-08:00","id":841723,"title":"Rules about Tattoos","content":"OK so does any one know of any rules about tattoos on Garou or any of the changing breeds after they have their first change and the like I know there are rules for tattoo fetishes. I'm wondering about normal every day Tattoos I have heard a few thoughts on the matter but any rules in the books would be nice to know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11413-megankitty","name":"Megankitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11413_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T22:38:45-08:00","id":841734,"title":"","content":"Welcome aboard, you can find rules for scar and tattoo fetishes in hammer and klaive I do believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T23:02:39-08:00","id":841740,"title":"","content":"I know about the Tattoo fetishes I am talking regular every day Tattoo because there is an on going argument about them and how you keep them as a Garou or changing breed some one says you need to dedicate the ink another says stay in breed form for 3 or 4 weeks and let it heal human slow and it should stay","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11413-megankitty","name":"Megankitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11413_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T23:13:11-08:00","id":841743,"title":"","content":"I would say however the rules for a tattoo fetish would apply apart from the binding a spirit into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T00:45:13-08:00","id":841771,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna go out on a limb and assume that you are talking about human form tattoos that show up in the other forms and do not end up covered in fur? If so, you will need to change the ink that's being used on you. I suggest The Rite of Spirit Awakening on the ink before you apply it of the Rite of Talisman Dedication during the application of the ink. If you just want it in human form, just get a normal tattoo.<br /> <br /> Nota bene, not having distinguishing marks on your battle forms is a net positive and will help you hide once the wetwork is done. Not everyone will freak out and forget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T06:29:13-08:00","id":841856,"title":"","content":"I think the OP is asking &quot;Does the Fera Regeneration expel/remove/eliminate tattoo ink?&quot; and the answer is no. Tattoos are not a wound, they're a foreign object embedded in the skin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T07:28:46-08:00","id":841876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/841723-rules-about-tattoos?p=841856#post841856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the OP is asking &quot;Does the Fera Regeneration expel/remove/eliminate tattoo ink?&quot; and the answer is no. Tattoos are not a wound, they're a foreign object embedded in the skin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll add a voice to the general gist (if not specific underlying rationale) for this. It's similar to how the Garou's regeneration doesn't cause earrings to be expelled from their ears -- it does heal damage/wounds, but only to a certain degree/extent relative to the over-arcing factors involved. However, it would reasonably be the case that -- for comparative example -- should the werewolf remove her earrings and then change to (or be in) a form that regenerates (which for most editions/settings would leave Metis always having this be the case), then the hole(s) would likely close over the course of just a few minutes/a scene (just as an ordinary person's would over a period of so many weeks/months, depending on fast a healer they are), requiring her to re-pierce them again (though, again, that's thematic to the ST's setting/Reality(tm), so YMMV). On that similar note, an &quot;ordinary&quot; tattoo that she might get would likely fade to a degree over time (just as ordinary mortal tattoos, depending on ink/detail/skill of the artist, can fade/distort over time... trust me, I've seen it happen too many times) that is notably faster than would be the case for humans -- likely much faster, again, if a Metis, and at least noticeably so if otherwise often assuming/remaining in a form that regenerates (as could be the case for a long-term umbral quest wherein staying &quot;battle-ready&quot; is part of the journey). So the more reasonable assessment is that most werewolves would have to have their mundane tattoos &quot;touched up&quot; much more frequently over the course of their lives than ordinary humans would (which, as I am typing this, reminds me that I need to get my 18 year-old tattoo touched up/tightened, color-wise/fine-detail-wise, as it is notably faded from when I got it originally... found an old pic of it from when I got it, and went &quot;Oh, yeah -- you looked great then... but *now*? -- a little weathered...&quot; ).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T07:35:06-08:00","id":841878,"title":"","content":"Actually the White Howlers Tribebook has the Rite of the Scared Tattoo. The tattoo serves to strengthen the connection between Garou and their Totem, providing an additional Totem power, depending on the spirit in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T10:03:36-08:00","id":841957,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Rite of Dedication&quot; is to 'dedicate' certain objects to travel sideways with the garou and disappear or adjust when the garou changes form. While the ST is encouraged to allow several objects to be counted as one, so that the limit of objects (equal to permanent gnosis) isn't hindering the game, the ST should also be aware, that this leeway isn't used to missuse the Rite.<br /> <br /> That said, there are certain things you don't need to dedicate, for it would be overly ridiculous: change in your dedicated wallet for example.<br /> Also, stepping sideways doesn't instantly clean the garou, by the logic that the dirt isn't dedicated.<br /> If it would, the garou would instantly make a hunger induced frenzy check after stepping sideways, for not-dedicated currently digested stomach content wouldn't side step either.<br /> <br /> So, hair dye, tattoos and similar 'contamination' of the skin is essentially a part of the garou and doesn't need dedication to travel to and from the umbra with the garou. Neither does any actual dirt or gore on the garou. That is not withstanding, that larger chunks of epherma will dissipate when in the material world and vice versa, but that still doesn't make the filth on your shirt disappear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T03:59:20-08:00","id":842474,"title":"","content":"I think we've answered quite a few potential questions here, and I'm not even sure what the OP was asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/a